    "content": "Vice President Ilyas Osman Lugatoor of Somalia's Puntland regional administration took part in the opening of the region's first date production exhibition, which was held to highlight the growing date palm sector. The event brought together local farmers, agricultural experts, and business representatives to display varieties of dates cultivated within Puntland and discuss ways to expand the industry.\n\nDate farming has long been practiced across parts of Puntland, but this exhibition marks a coordinated effort to formalize and scale up production. The regional government aims to reduce reliance on imported dates, particularly during Ramadan when demand spikes, and to tap into export markets. Officials say the initiative aligns with broader economic strategies to diversify Puntland's sources of revenue beyond livestock and trade.\n\nThe vice president's participation signals high-level political backing for the agricultural sector, which has historically received limited state support. Organizers expect that events like this will encourage private investment, improve farming techniques, and connect producers with both domestic and international buyers. This includes members of the Somali diaspora, who often send remittances and may seek investment opportunities in sectors like agribusiness.\n\nFor Somali communities abroad, the development could mean better access to high-quality Puntland dates and a chance to invest in a rising industry that offers both cultural ties and financial returns. The exhibition also serves as a bridge between local producers and global markets, presenting a practical avenue for economic engagement with the region.\n\nAs Puntland continues to build its agricultural profile, such showcases are expected to become annual events, creating a platform for knowledge exchange and trade expansion. The government has pledged to provide technical support to farmers and to improve water management and processing facilities to ensure consistent output.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/puntland-oo-caalamka-u-soo-bandhigtay-wax-soo-saarkeeda-timirta/425315/",
